<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!-- Select the device icon pack by default.

         IconPackStore.getCurrent() reads the com.android.launcher3.prefs
         preference `pref_iconPackPackage` and falls back to
         R.string.icon_pack_default_pkg, whose upstream value is the sentinel
         "android" meaning "system icons"
         (packages/apps/Trebuchet/iconloaderlib/res/values/lineage_config.xml:19,
         read at IconPackStore.java:68). Overriding it here makes the pack the
         default on a fresh /data while leaving Home settings -> Icon pack fully
         functional: the user can still pick "System icons" or any pack they
         install, and their choice wins because it is stored in the preference.

         THE PATH MATTERS AND TWO NEARBY ONES DO NOT WORK.
         * quickstep/res is a LOCAL_RESOURCE_DIR of the TrebuchetQuickStep
           package (Trebuchet/Android.mk:217-219), which is the launcher
           vendor/lineage actually ships, so DEVICE_PACKAGE_OVERLAYS reaches it
           (package_internal.mk:135-159) and aapt2 takes the last -R.
         * overlay/packages/apps/Trebuchet/res/... is SILENTLY IGNORED: that
           res dir belongs to Launcher3CommonDepsLib, a static java library, and
           Make applies DEVICE_PACKAGE_OVERLAYS only to BUILD_PACKAGE modules.
         * overlay/packages/apps/Trebuchet/iconloaderlib/res/... does work, and
           must not be used: SystemUI and PermissionController link that same
           Soong android_library, so the override would leak into how THEY
           render legacy app icons. -->
    <string name="icon_pack_default_pkg" translatable="false">org.lineageos.iconpack.k50sv1</string>
</resources>
